<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/5th-century-bce">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Battle</p><h1 class="enc-title">Battle of Mantinea (418 BCE)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">418 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/5th-century-bce">5th century BCE</a> · Also known as First Battle of Mantinea · Part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Battle of Mantinea of 418 BCE was the largest land battle of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnesian-war">Peloponnesian War</a>, fought in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arcadia">Arcadia</a>. A Spartan army under King Agis II defeated an alliance of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argo">Argos</a>, Mantinea and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/athens">Athens</a> that had been formed to challenge Spartan dominance in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peloponnese">Peloponnese</a>. The victory restored <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sparta">Sparta</a>'s prestige, and Mantinea was forced back into alliance with it.</p></div>
